 Ballarat, Victoria"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/255095"} "30 from 15 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Of all of podium finishers in the K-2 1000 from the 1952 Summer Olympics, only " [:a {:href "/athletes/9088"} "Max Raub"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9106"} "Herbert Wiedermann"] " of Austria, the bronze medalists, travelled to the 1956 edition to compete again. Similarly, the only recent World medalists were Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/9955"} "Meinrad Miltenberger"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9970"} "Michel Scheuer"] ", the 1950 runners-up, the latter of whom had taken bronze in the K-1 10000 the previous day. Finland, the defending Olympic champion, was represented by " [:a {:href "/athletes/9557"} "Pentti Raaskoski"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9534"} "Juhani Helenius"] ", while Hungary, the reigning World Champion, sent " [:a {:href "/athletes/10114"} "Imre Vágyóczky"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10099"} "Zoltán Szigeti"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the first opening heat, the Soviet duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10982"} "Mihhail Kaaleste"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10953"} "Anatoly Demitkov"] " secured a victory over the Austrians and helped eliminate the Hungarians, while the Germans won the second, easier heat. In the final heat, Raaskoski and Helenius were disqualified after running into Belgians " [:a {:href ""} "Rik Verbrugghe"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9153"} "Germain Van De Moere"] ", while Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/8996"} "Walter Brown"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/9010"} "Dennis Green"] ", who had won bronze in the K-2 10000 the day before, emerged victorious. In the medal round, Miltenberger and Scheuer captured the gold medal in Olympic record time, while Kaaleste and Demitkov came in shortly after for silver. The rest of the field was fairly far back, and it was Miltenberger and Scheuer who nabbed the bronze, stealing it from the Romanian duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/10569"} "Mircea Anastasescu"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/10621"} "Stavru Teodorov"] " by only 0.3 seconds."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9970"} "Michel Scheuer"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9955"} "Meinrad Miltenberger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "3:56.4 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:49.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Best"} "OB"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10982"} "Mihhail Kaaleste"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10953"} "Anatoly Demitkov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "3:55.1 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "3:51.4 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/9088"} "Max Raub"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/9106"} "Herbert Wiedermann"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUT"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUT.png"}] "AUT"]] [:td {} "3:57.2 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "3:55.8 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/10569"} "Mircea Anastasescu"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/10621"} "Stavru Teodorof"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RO